\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T13:57:03-07:00","id":908583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/908549-faerie-worse-than-hell?p=908562#post908562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I'm sorry, to clarify. The unicorn started telling the story and was telling it while a True Fae ate it (cannibalized it) and smeared its rainbow blood everywhere? Am I reading the situation correctly?</div> </div> </div> </div>The narrator is none of the entities in the shot, rather being a demon in a bar who'd been to Faerie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T14:01:06-07:00","id":908591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/908549-faerie-worse-than-hell?p=908583#post908583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The narrator is none of the entities in the shot, rather being a demon in a bar who'd been to Faerie.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a bit less creepy and dissonant than I thought it was.<br /> <br /> That being said, I do agree with the comics, yes, and now I want to go buy this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T14:03:26-07:00","id":908596,"title":"","content":"The problem is the last part of the comic<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://3.bp.blogspot.com/-2Wegfrvckqg/VuIJ0Jg7EiI/AAAAAAAAFms/bsWk6sSdfFkMlyC98VyX_1c96FSR9QNEw/s640/IMG_0499.PNG\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> I know he is godamn Constantine, but come on, these fairies are idiots! If only the Gentry in WoD was so easy to fool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T14:05:32-07:00","id":908603,"title":"","content":"The answer to the question is yes. Faerie is so, so much worse than Hell. Demons have rules. They have guidelines. You beat them, that's usually it, end of story. They might hold a grudge, but a demon will follow their bargains and if you managed to find a way out of it they probably won't seek retribution for it. You beat the Fae, find a loophole in a Pledge and play that card for all it's worth? They aren't ticked off, they're delighted. They'll come after you again not for vengeance, but because they know you can play the game- and this time, they'll play to <i>win</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T14:50:57-07:00","id":908633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/908549-faerie-worse-than-hell?p=908562#post908562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I'm sorry, to clarify. The unicorn started telling the story and was telling it while a True Fae ate it (cannibalized it) and smeared its rainbow blood everywhere? Am I reading the situation correctly?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think a Demon was telling the story the whole time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T14:59:36-07:00","id":908641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/908549-faerie-worse-than-hell?p=908633#post908633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a Demon was telling the story the whole time.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it was second hand account made by Constantine. He summoned the demon, he asked the question, he got lifted by the throat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T15:18:57-07:00","id":908653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/908549-faerie-worse-than-hell?p=908596#post908596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is the last part of the comic<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://3.bp.blogspot.com/-2Wegfrvckqg/VuIJ0Jg7EiI/AAAAAAAAFms/bsWk6sSdfFkMlyC98VyX_1c96FSR9QNEw/s640/IMG_0499.PNG\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> I know he is godamn Constantine, but come on, these fairies are idiots! If only the Gentry in WoD was so easy to fool.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't think the Gentry would so easily taken out with one punch either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T15:59:20-07:00","id":908678,"title":"","content":"Unless they want to.<br /> <br /> After all it makes for a good story to be tricked by a pesky human then enact terrible vengeance on him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T16:14:42-07:00","id":908690,"title":"","content":"Notice the snap there? The neck broke.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T17:36:58-07:00","id":908743,"title":"","content":"1) Ah Constantine. Seeing it puts me in a new hurry to continue with Hellblazer and none of the new incarnation. We'll see when we get there.<br /> <br /> 2) Speaking of Hellblazer, I don't know. I would have to see more of Faerie before I could make the comparison, but Hell'sblazer's hell gets rather viciously mean. It does have rules though, and it does have the acute sense of self that the demon describes.<br /> <br /> 3) Outside of Hellblazer but not in Chronicles, it's debatable, given how many variations there are and how many of those variations are actually Hell and fae realms being laid on top of one another.<br /> <br /> 4) In Chronicles, there's a couple of analogs, but I'm gonna cheap out and make the primary analog the Inferno, because it's easy and it's fan-pleasing to acknowledge that, yes, Inferno exists.<br /> <br /> So, Is Arcadia worse than the Inferno?<br /> <br /> Yes. A thousand stories and a thousand thousand tears over, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T18:37:51-07:00","id":908779,"title":"","content":"Demons need your bloody thumbprint to seal a bargain, given of your own free will. They have eons of experience in human wants and needs, but at the end of the day, they win by coercing you into ignoring your better judgement. As your life burns down around you, you will have no one to really blame for that except yourself. You will understand what happened.<br /> <br /> The Fae are only interested in the here and now, and if you have the audacity to not give in to their every whim, they will take your better judgment and mutilate it until you cannot tell the difference between <i><b>their</b></i> wants and <i><b>your</b></i> needs. They care nothing for the sanctity of your body, mind or soul. If you do not fight tooth and nail for your right to be yourself, you will soon lose the capacity to discern the real from the imagined. To get but a moment's high, <b><i>they will make you like them.</i></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 06-06-2016, 09:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T21:03:42-07:00","id":908867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/908549-faerie-worse-than-hell?p=908779#post908779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demons need your bloody thumbprint to seal a bargain, given of your own free will. They have eons of experience in human wants and needs, but at the end of the day, they win by coercing you into ignoring your better judgement. As your life burns down around you, you will have no one to really blame for that except yourself. You will understand what happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, while that's an ideal circumstance, a demon could just as easily tempt someone else into sacrificing your soul to it. But there's those with two Vices and a lack of a Virtue, demonologists and explorers of sin, cenobites of vice. 'Hell' in Chronicles of Darkness seems to take some inspiration from Hellraiser, where Hell can be a haven for the wicked. Better to rule and whatnot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Fae are only interested in the here and now, and if you have the audacity to not give in to their every whim, they will take your better judgment and mutilate it until you cannot tell the difference between <i><b>their</b></i> wants and <i><b>your</b></i> needs. They care nothing for the sanctity of your body, mind or soul. If you do not fight tooth and nail for your right to be yourself, you will soon lose the capacity to discern the real from the imagined. To get but a moment's high, <b><i>they will make you like them.</i></b> </div> </div> </div>The Changeling in Lost don't seem to take much inspiration from modern media, as far as I can tell. The True Fae seem out to enjoy themselves and live their story, while their victims just become part of the scene, even their potential escape might have been part of the story, waiting to end in a later act. At least going with the Fae as stories thing idea. One of the other options was having them be demons, in which case Arcadia is hell. Either way, yeah, it is worse, like children toying with insects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-07-2016, 12:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T16:37:22-07:00","id":912516,"title":"","content":"There's this hypothesis about the True Fae presented in Autumn Nightmares that says they were angels who did not side with God or Lucifer during the War In Heaven. They were barred from Heaven, but not sent to Hell, so they wandered the Earth, absorbing human traits they were not made to process until it drove them mad. Arcadia, then, is a disjointed attempt at recreating their home, but the horrors of Hell entered in one way or another. <br /> <br /> This makes Arcadia a sort of inconstant Purgatory, which would explain why it can be escaped, and why there is both splendor and torment. But without a central authority watching the process of redemption/second chances that is usually associated with Purgatory, there is no guarantee of consistency in the delights and punishments.<br /> <br /> This opens some interesting possibilities that only now have occurred to me. Perhaps changelings can move closer to their demonic or angelic sides, such as they are, and develop unusual powers represented by unique Goblin Contracts and Goblin Vows.<br /> <br /> Who knows, maybe Becoming Nightmare as described in Equinox Road can be modified to represent a descent into ruling over Hell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T17:19:23-07:00","id":912538,"title":"","content":"I just remembered that there is already homebrew themed around Heaven and Hell: the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/226145-index-of-fan-made-changeling-material\"><b>Contracts Of The Cross and the Contracts Of The Inferno</b></a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T06:11:52-07:00","id":912759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/908549-faerie-worse-than-hell?p=908560#post908560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crap now I want to know what kind of pleasure he was offering the fairy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The sweet release of death!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T19:41:18-07:00","id":914586,"title":"","content":"Faeries has one very important mercy that Hell does not. It allows you to leave. Oh, its not easy, and the things IN Faeries might take actions to stop you, but the Realm itself doesn't prevent you from leaving if you remember the way home (e.g. if you are still human enough). By all accounts Inferno actively makes it hard to get out, and usually requires intervention from the outside before one can exit. Remember, of the two Faerie is not the place the requires those who enter to abandon all hope. <br /> <br /> Now, whether or not having a little hope to cling to makes Faerie all the more crueler than hell? I'll leave that for you to decide. <br /> <br /> Of course, if you go to hell its usually because you deserve it. Inferno is no exception in this regard. Faerie, on the other hand, is far more &quot;welcoming&quot;. It will take you in any place, any time, and it has no prerequisites or requirements. Sinners and saints, young and old, good men and bad. Faeries accepts them all. Whether they want to go or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T20:10:25-07:00","id":914599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/908549-faerie-worse-than-hell?p=914586#post914586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Faeries has one very important mercy that Hell does not. It allows you to leave. Oh, its not easy, and the things IN Faeries might take actions to stop you, but the Realm itself doesn't prevent you from leaving if you remember the way home (e.g. if you are still human enough). By all accounts Inferno actively makes it hard to get out, and usually requires intervention from the outside before one can exit. Remember, of the two Faerie is not the place the requires those who enter to abandon all hope.<br /> <br /> Now, whether or not having a little hope to cling to makes Faerie all the more crueler than hell? I'll leave that for you to decide.<br /> <br /> Of course, if you go to hell its usually because you deserve it. Inferno is no exception in this regard. Faerie, on the other hand, is far more &quot;welcoming&quot;. It will take you in any place, any time, and it has no prerequisites or requirements. Sinners and saints, young and old, good men and bad. Faeries accepts them all. Whether they want to go or not.</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GUeBMwn_eYc\" data-code=\"GUeBMwn_eYc\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/GUeBMwn_eYc/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T18:44:54-07:00","id":917089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/908549-faerie-worse-than-hell?p=914586#post914586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Faeries has one very important mercy that Hell does not. It allows you to leave. Oh, its not easy, and the things IN Faeries might take actions to stop you, but the Realm itself doesn't prevent you from leaving if you remember the way home (e.g. if you are still human enough). By all accounts Inferno actively makes it hard to get out, and usually requires intervention from the outside before one can exit. Remember, of the two Faerie is not the place the requires those who enter to abandon all hope.<br /> <br /> Now, whether or not having a little hope to cling to makes Faerie all the more crueler than hell? I'll leave that for you to decide.<br /> <br /> Of course, if you go to hell its usually because you deserve it. Inferno is no exception in this regard. Faerie, on the other hand, is far more &quot;welcoming&quot;. It will take you in any place, any time, and it has no prerequisites or requirements. Sinners and saints, young and old, good men and bad. Faeries accepts them all. Whether they want to go or not.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hell can't be that hard to escape from. Demons seem to break out of it all the time! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T14:11:17-07:00","id":918795,"title":"","content":"Do some people actually go to the Inferno after they die? I thought it was a just sort of a weird un-place that non-God Machine demons come from. <br /> <br /> Chronicles of Darkness tends to be rather vague about the afterlife in general, especially considering that souls don't really contain a person's personality or sense of self, and ghosts are generally thought to be incomplete echoes of a person rather than a continuation of that person's existence after death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 06-21-2016, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T14:34:30-07:00","id":918805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/908549-faerie-worse-than-hell?p=918795#post918795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do some people actually go to the Inferno after they die? I thought it was a just sort of a weird un-place that non-God Machine demons come from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Larvals are 'evil ghosts,' created when people die when targeted or possessed by a Whisperer, or after making a demonic pact. While Twilight is their natural state, based on the similar rules for spirits, 'expelling' a Larval wouldn't send it to the Underworld, but to the Inferno.<br /> <br /> Considering they can evolve into higher ranked Infernal demons, they could likely be brought back in a more 'true' demonic form.<br /> <br /> Not exactly the same as going to Inferno when someone dies, but it's there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T13:13:38-07:00","id":921648,"title":"","content":"I got a real vibe of the comic <i>Saga</i> from the art of Faerie here... Will for sure be using that as an artistic way of showing my players what Arcadia may look and feel like at times. Also love the thoughts on Arcadia being a flawed recreation of Heaven made by corrupted angels.<br /> <br /> I agree the Constantine Arcadia may exist like shown in some places, especially for the Fairest (1st edition). I read somewhere that Fairest wake up from nightmares about Arcadia and they feel wrong and guilt by how much pleasure and how good it was there among the pain. As Clarity drops we also know that many changelings want to go back and feel those sensations that reality just cannot give them.<br /> <br /> I wonder if this type of Arcadia will change for 2nd edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}